{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.low_mode_block_global","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.low_mode_block_global","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeBlock.cumulative_enstrophy_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeBlock.cumulative_enstrophy_bound","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/low_mode_block_global.lean#L85-L112","doc":"**The discrete Leray energy inequality**: with quantitative\ndissipation `E (n+1) ≤ E n − δν·Ω n` and nonnegative energy, the\ncumulative enstrophy is bounded by the initial energy:\n`δν·∑_{i<n} Ω i ≤ E 0` for every `n`.  Enstrophy is\nsummable-in-time against the dissipation rate — the discrete\ncounterpart of the classical Leray a-priori bound, again with no\nsmallness hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeBlock.block_global_enstrophy_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeBlock.block_global_enstrophy_bound","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/low_mode_block_global.lean#L69-L83","doc":"**Large-data global enstrophy bound at the fixed block**: energy\nmonotonicity + finite-block norm equivalence give\n`Ω n ≤ kmax²·E 0` for every `n` — no smallness hypothesis on the\ndata.  (The bound is uniform in time and in the data scale `E 0`,\nbut grows with the block's top wavenumber — see the module\ndocstring for the `ε`-non-uniformity localization.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeBlock.energy_le_initial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeBlock.energy_le_initial","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/low_mode_block_global.lean#L61-L67","doc":"Monotone energy stays below its initial value. ","signatureChunk":0}]}